.TH PGN-LIST 1 "November 2026" "pgn-list" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pgn-list \- list players and details from PGN games
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pgn-list
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR [\fIFILE ...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pgn-list
prints one line for each chess game in one or more PGN files. Each line shows
the players and ratings, site, year, ECO code, and result.
.PP
.nf
club.pgn: Doe 2750 - Carlsen 2830 | Wijk aan Zee | 2024 | A22 | 1-0
.fi
.PP
If a player name uses the PGN form "Surname, Given name", only the part before
the comma is shown. Other names are shown as written. Missing names, site,
year, or ECO appear as "?".  Result markers in the moves take
priority over the Result tag; a missing or unknown result is shown as "*".
Player, site, and ECO fields are limited to 32 bytes, including "..." when
shortened. Input file names are shown in full.
.PP
Use the file name
.B -
to read standard input. At least one file name is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -n , " " --no-filename
Omit the file name at the start of each output line.
.TP
.B --strict
Stop after the first file that cannot be read or parsed. Without this option,
the program reports the error and continues with later files.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage and options.
.TP
.B -?
Show the same help as --help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the version number.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is 0 when all requested inputs are listed, and 2 if an input
cannot be read or parsed or the command line is invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pgn-count (1),
.BR pgn-reverse (1)
